# Voice settings used by make_vo.py for every episode (build_ep.sh exports them; PLAYBOOK shows the manual command).
# A = owner-picked voice (chosen again on 26 Oct 22:19 over B/C/D): Kokoro 75% am_eric + 25% am_fenrir, lifted register
# ~165 Hz, expressive prosody. Refine A (pace, pauses, stress, phrasing) — never swap the blend or drop the lift.
# 26 Oct 22:50 refinement (voice lab, carrot script): SPD 0.88 / PZ 1.6 / PMIN 0.3 -> UTMOS 4.27 -> 4.36, 213 -> 197 wpm.
# Any change must pass engine/tools/voice_report.py (UTMOS naturalness not lower, ASR clean) and be logged in improvements.md.
# 27 Oct 22:46 IST owner: "make the voice more mature, more natural" -> the A lock is lifted. Voice lab on the onion lines
# (i1-b1, same text, all 0 ASR errors): A 4.450 / line mean 4.388 / 173 Hz / 192 wpm; M1 (michael/onyx/fenrir/echo) 4.480 / 4.415 /
# 119 Hz; M2 (michael .4 / puck .3 / eric .3, own register, fuller prosody) 4.488 / 4.419 / 135 Hz / 174 wpm  <- best + adopted;
# M3 4.443; M4 (michael/eric/fenrir = the OopsMyBusiness voice) 4.478 -> avoided so the channels sound different.
# M2 = a grown-up, warm, calm-confident guy. Keep the blend; refine pace / pauses / stress like before. Pace gate now 165-195 wpm.
VMIX=am_michael:0.4,am_puck:0.3,am_eric:0.3
GT=0
SPD=0.88
PZ=1.6
PMIN=0.3
EXS=0.9
BMP=1.0
STR=1.0
# 27 Oct (ep 12) A/B on the silver script, same lines: ported the studio R&D per-line prosody gate (PGATE 0.15: a line that loses
# > 0.15 UTMOS to our PSOLA moves vs its flat take is re-rendered at 0.6 / 0.3 strength) -> chunk20 4.350 -> 4.412,
# line mean 4.292 -> 4.339, pace 186 wpm kept. SPLIT (one Kokoro call per sentence + gap) did NOT help this blend
# (4.365 / 4.315 at 0.12, 4.362 / 4.325 at 0.06) and slowed speech to 170-173 wpm (< 180 gate) -> off for FreshNestHub.
PGATE=0.15
SPLIT=0
# 27 Oct (ep 13) A/B on the onion script, same lines + same rewrites: lighter pitch processing EXS 0.5/BMP 0.8 -> 0.4/0.7
# (backlog "less audible pitch processing"): chunk20 4.420 -> 4.428, line mean 4.347 -> 4.350, whole first-100 s 4.281 -> 4.321,
# f0 range 17.8 -> 17.2 st (gate >= 15), pace 190 wpm both -> adopted (small, within noise: re-check on the next script).
# 28 Oct (ep 15, first full M2 episode): chunk20 4.499 / line mean 4.459 (ep 14 A voice 4.412 / 4.344), 172 wpm, f0 16.6 st.
# STR 1.15 A/B on the same text = 4.497 / 4.456 (neutral) -> STR stays 1.0.
# 31 Oct (ep 17, first ink episode): script REGISTERS per beat (per-line base st in vo_lines: asides -0.6 + speed 0.95, reveals +1.2, plain +0.4)
# A/B vs uniform +0.8 on the same take: chunk20 4.508 vs 4.507, line mean 4.465 vs 4.461 -> keep; the engine settings above are unchanged.
# 31 Oct (ep 18): DROP-STRESS markup ('word:dn' in vo_lines stressed words = -2 st + longer, already supported by make_vo) A/B on the same take vs
# lift-stress: chunk20 4.502 vs 4.494, line mean 4.465 vs 4.468 (neutral) -> use it on deadpan payoff words; engine settings above unchanged.
# Shipped ep 18: chunk20 4.509 / line mean 4.479 (new best), 169.7 wpm, f0 17.3 st. Lesson: keep the hook QUESTION in one breath (no '...' inside it).
